WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:06.960
One of the things we've been following since the&nbsp;
January 6th Trump riots has been the involvement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:15.680
of law enforcement and or military in the riots.&nbsp;
And we now are starting to see numbers attached&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:22.720
to this that are not particularly reassuring&nbsp;
about the US military. Active military personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:30.240
and veterans are overrepresented. Looking at the&nbsp;
first 150 arrests and records released about what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:37.120
took place on January 6th, CNN did an analysis&nbsp;
of Pentagon records and court proceedings and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:46.960
found that 14 percent of the first 150 arrests&nbsp;
are of current or former members of the U.S.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:53.520
military. That's more than doubled the proportion&nbsp;
of servicemen and women in the population. That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.520 --> 00:01:00.160
calculated based on Census Bureau and Department&nbsp;
of Defense Statistics. Back in 2013, there were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:06.240
one point three million active duty members of the&nbsp;
services and 18 million veterans together. That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:13.120
five point nine percent of the population. And yet&nbsp;
14 percent of those arrested are members, current&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:20.880
or former of some branch of the U.S. military.&nbsp;
Two of those are army to our National Guard. Of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:27.520
the seventeen veterans, six are former Army aide&nbsp;
or former Marines, two are former Navy. One was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:33.680
in the Air Force, at least one served in Vietnam.&nbsp;
Others tended to be deployed to Afghanistan and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:39.280
Iraq, which makes sense from the standpoint&nbsp;
of age. At least one earned a Purple Heart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:45.600
discharged at a variety of ranks and included&nbsp;
officers as well, a captain and a lieutenant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:52.880
colonel. So there's a few different issues here.
First of all, just from like a very abstract&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:57.840
historical standpoint, if you're&nbsp;
at all familiar with Roman history,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:07.120
there's sort of like a classic Roman historical&nbsp;
idea of disgruntled soldiers supporting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:12.560
their leader, their emperor, for a coup attempt.
And so I don't know that we need to go the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:18.960
whole sort of sort of poetic route with this or&nbsp;
historical analogies. But they are certainly there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:27.040
and it's not an unprecedented thing. One question&nbsp;
I have is this particular study from Pentagon data&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:35.520
done by CNN is military, current and former. If we&nbsp;
were to say military and law enforcement, I wonder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:41.680
where the number goes to from 14 percent. That's&nbsp;
that's one question. But this is a well known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:46.640
sort of historical element that that&nbsp;
repeats itself. And to be very clear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:52.560
this isn't about saying troops are bad as&nbsp;
people in principle there are. I mean, listen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:59.840
you can even say that these are victims, right?
If you understand the idea that there is a massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:07.600
adaptation problem for people post military&nbsp;
service, this seems to be more of a vulnerability.&nbsp;

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:13.200
When we talk to I mean, I'm not making an analogy&nbsp;
here between white supremacists and former members&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:18.800
of the military. But what I do think is important&nbsp;
to understand is that after traumatic experiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:23.600
or during them, people become vulnerable to&nbsp;
really bad ideas and to be sucked in by cults.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:31.200
And every former white supremacist we've talked&nbsp;
to, every former KKK person we've talked to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:37.040
has told us essentially the same story about they&nbsp;
were in a vulnerable place. And just as they fell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.520
for the community granted to them by the ideas of&nbsp;
white supremacy, because that's what was going on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:45.920
around them, they could have been pulled in by&nbsp;
a religion. They could have been pulled in by by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:52.400
almost anything. And we know that there are lots&nbsp;
of folks who serve in the military and they have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:59.680
a difficulty adapting to post military life.&nbsp;
And you could fall into any number of different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:04.400
things. So this is not about simply saying&nbsp;
that the people are bad people necessarily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:10.080
but there might be some explanation here as&nbsp;
to why the Trampas thought that if they do the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:16.080
insurrection and they try to steal the election&nbsp;
for Trump, that maybe the military would stand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:21.680
down. Is it possible because. They themselves,&nbsp;
as members of the military, current or former,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:24.960
thought that maybe that's something that&nbsp;
would happen, that maybe the military&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:30.800
would join them in the insurrection. I don't&nbsp;
know. I'm thinking out loud here, but the numbers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:37.120
are certainly stunning, you know, more than a&nbsp;
2x representation relative to the population&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:43.200
of current and former military. And I don't I&nbsp;
mean, you tell me whether this is too cynical.&nbsp;

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:49.360
Is it conceivable that they may have been targeted&nbsp;
on social media? I mean, we know at this point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:56.960
the degree to which campaigns can be targeted to&nbsp;
folks so narrowly on social media. Is it possible?

